        <headline>Gale Warning issued September 25 at 7:34AM EDT until September 26 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Baltimore MD/Washington DC</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Small Craft Advisory, north winds 15 to 25 kt
with gusts up to 30 kt. For the Gale Warning, north winds 20
to 25 kt with gusts up to 35 kt and waves 2 to 4 ft expected.

* WHERE...Choptank River to Cambridge MD and the Little Choptank
River and Patuxent River to Broomes Island MD.

* WHEN...For the Small Craft Advisory, until 6 AM EDT Saturday.
For the Gale Warning, from 6 AM to 6 PM EDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous waves which could
capsize or damage vessels.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for hazardous conditions.</instruction>
